[{:db/id "q-89876/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "d6f09894-745c-5512-a3a4-f3906fb13303" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89876/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "f57cf218-7869-5a35-8824-d99a645722e0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89876/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "cff59460-e010-5a83-830f-5102724fe809" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89876/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "4fc253ea-4ae9-5a7b-8f0e-f1d499dc9c10" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89876/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer/id #uuid "aadac8fe-099c-5fce-b6ea-f4485731b705" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89876/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "80d5d792-c634-530d-b38f-581f783df1f7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-89876/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-89876/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-89876/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-89876/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-89876/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" "q-89876/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-89876" :question/id #uuid "b03dd7a9-474a-5ef8-b096-f3a65f8f342e" :question/math-academy-id "q-89876" :question/problem "The function $y=f(x)$ satisfies the differential equation \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=y+2x.\n$$\n\n \n\nGiven that the point $P(0,-1)$ lies on the graph of the function, evaluate $\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}$ at $P.$" :question/worked-solution "To find an expression for the second derivative, we differentiate the equation with respect to $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y+2x) \\\\ \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2x) \\\\ \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x) \\\\ \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute the given expression for $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ into the above and simplify the resulting expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =(y+2x)+2 \\\\ \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =y+2x+2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute the coordinates of our point into the above expression for the second derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}|}_{(0,-1)} & ={(y+2x+2)|}_{(0,-1)} \\\\  & =-1+2(0)+2 \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-89876/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f28fbcc-6d9c-5dc7-89cc-13255db78765"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-89876"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-89884/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "863cac10-f49c-5934-9897-1c0082fdec93" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89884/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408a